.TH CHM-BINARY-INSPECT 1
.SH NAME
chm-binary-inspect \- inspect executable headers without executing the file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chm-binary-inspect
.RI [ --json ] " FILE..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
Identifies ELF, PE/COFF, Mach-O thin and universal, and WebAssembly file headers. Reports architecture, bitness, endianness where applicable, object type or subsystem, and file size. The inspector reads header metadata only; it does not load, execute, emulate, or certify the binary.
.SH SAFETY
File-format recognition is not a trust decision. Do not execute untrusted files. Check signatures, provenance, hashes, architecture, ABI, dependencies, and license terms before installation or compatibility execution.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when all files were recognized; 1 when one or more files were unrecognized, truncated, or unreadable; 2 for invalid command-line usage.
